\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Longitudinal dynamical structure factor at all eight FCC-32 momenta for $J_{\pm }/J_{zz}=-0.20$. (a) Naive periodic dynamics and (b) the transport-masked theory use the same depth-$d=1$ space, 120 final states, four sublattice probes, Gaussian width $\eta /J_{zz}=1.2\times 10^{-3}$, and common color scale. Periodic dynamics produces strong inelastic response at $\Gamma $ and a higher apparent excitation scale. The mask removes the $\Gamma $ response while retaining finite weight at every nonzero momentum.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dssf}{{2}{4}{Longitudinal dynamical structure factor at all eight FCC-32 momenta for $\Jpm /\Jzz =-0.20$. (a) Naive periodic dynamics and (b) the transport-masked theory use the same depth-$d=1$ space, 120 final states, four sublattice probes, Gaussian width $\eta /\Jzz =1.2\times 10^{-3}$, and common color scale. Periodic dynamics produces strong inelastic response at $\Gamma $ and a higher apparent excitation scale. The mask removes the $\Gamma $ response while retaining finite weight at every nonzero momentum}{figure.2}{}}
